 <iati-activity default-currency="USD" hierarchy="1" iati-activities:version="2.03" xml:lang="EN" xmlns:iati-activities="http://d-portal.org/xmlns/iati-activities">
  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-VNM128</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved national capacity to formulate and implement evidence-based policies, strategies for inclusive, transformative and sustainable agriculture, industry and service sectors</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For the promotion of the productivity ecosystem for decent work, ILO works towards bringing more productivity-focused provisions into the revision of the employment law during this biennium. This includes the provision of technical support to the roll-out of the newly adopted National Programme for Improving Labour Productivity 2023-2030 by Viet Nam.

In addition, Viet Nam is among the first developing countries in the Asia and the Pacific region to implement the new labour statistics standards from the 19th International Conference of Labour Statisticians (19th ICLS, 2013), so that its labour market data could better serve its employment law and policies. However, the country has not yet implemented the subsequent standards on work relationships from the 20th ICLS (2018), as well as the new standards for statistics on the informal economy (21st ICLS, 2023), an important policy topic for the country. The ILO supports  the country in implementing these latest statistical standards during the 2024-2025 biennium</narrative>
  </description>
